	(text "Every part: its value as printed, what it is, its nets, whether it is fitted and where it is drawn. A\nreference on the drawing leads to its row, the row back to it."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 27.94 256.54 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.75 1.75)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "0d2da03e-6b98-504e-bf37-70e3d890d0da")
	)
	(text "How to read it"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 215.9 40.64 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "68e7bebe-0a8e-5bd3-b086-91bace0e9724")
	)
	(text "Click a box on the left to open its page. \"Contents\" and the page numbers at the bottom\nright of every page lead back here and to each page.\n\nCyan lines are connections: wires and pin ends, all one width. A dot joins lines; a cross\non a pin end means the pin is not connected. Pins connect by net labels (the boxed names):\npins whose labels carry the same name are on one net, on any page.\n[3/C4] after a label: page 3 carries that net too, its label in zone C4 (column 4, row C of\nthe border). Click it to land on that label. No [page/zone]: the net is on this page only.\nClick a part's reference to find its row in the parts list; the row's page/zone leads back.\nA part crossed out in red is not fitted (DNP). White: parts and their references. Grey:\nvalues, pin names, pin numbers. A dashed frame is a block of the circuit, titled at its top\nleft. An amber K3 marks a Kleidos addition or correction; click it for its row below."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 215.9 45.085 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.75 1.75)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "005eefce-b2f8-5cc3-bb52-6d32e5d77d74")
	)
	(text "Notes"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 215.9 87.135 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "7cf943f6-67f4-5c24-a895-b848ad752526")
	)
	(text "Every part, pin and net of the CoreS3-SE's netlist, with the values the vendor documents:\nconnectivity documented from the vendor's public documentation, with Kleidos additions and\ncorrections listed on page 1 (M5Stack's Sch_M5_CoreS3_SE_v1.0 schematic, 2025-06-03, and\nits docs page, cited in README.md and netlist.yaml beside this file). Layout and symbols are\nthis project's. No footprints, no PCB, no part numbers beyond the documented ones.\nPages 2 to 7 are the vendor's sheets 1 to 6, in order. The parts the vendor's print greys\nout (camera connector, MPU6886, BMI270, BMM150) are not in the SE's netlist and are not\ndrawn. Values are as the vendor prints them (10K/1%, 22uF 6.3V). A value of NC means not\nfitted: those parts are marked DNP. Reference designators are the vendor's; BAT1 is printed\nBAT1/NC. Nets the vendor left unnamed carry names of ours (AXP_LX1, BOOT_RC...).\nZones: columns 1-8 and rows A-F, 50 mm apart, printed in the border."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 215.9 91.58 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.75 1.75)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "f16fa1d9-51fd-560d-8652-c28b9a1baf3c")
	)
